or": false, "num_turns": 5, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "12 of the 150 rules didn't match their docstrings. I fixed all of them in `pricebook.py`, and changed only the calculation code, never the docstrings.\n\nTo check, I wrote a script that reads each rule's docstring and works out the expected price from it. It compared every rule against that for quantities 0–259 and nine different unit prices. Before the fix it flagged exactly these 12 rules; after the fix it flags none.\n\n| Rule | What was wrong | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 07, 141, 142 | The cap was applied to the price, then the % taken (`min(base, cap) * pct`) | Take the % first, then cap the discount |\n| 133 | Same problem on a marginal rule (`min((qty-5)*unit, cap) * pct`) | Take the % first, then cap the discount |\n| 16, 105 | The discount started at 101+ units instead of 100+ | Changed the threshold to `>= 100` |\n| 37 | The discount started at 6+ units instead of 5+ | Changed the threshold to `>= 5` |\n| 19, 92 | The discount was rounded (`round(... / 100)`) instead of rounded down | Changed to `// 100` (round down to the won) |\n| 111, 124 | Marked \"marginal\" but discounted every unit | Discount only the units above the threshold (`(qty - threshold) * unit`) |\n| 125 | The docstring says 5% but the code used 6% | Changed to 5% |\n\nSTATUS: DONE", "ttft_ms": 1677, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 26288, "uuid": "590e2ec5-f2e7-412f-b1f0-03d45ba93d1e", "ttft_stream_ms": 1080, "time_to_request_ms": 364, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 8, "system_prompt": 12, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 3, "input_hooks": 1, "transcript_persist": 14, "tool_pool_refresh": 2, "init_message": 3, "engine_pickup": 0, "message_prep": 1, "model_config_wait": 0, "autocompact": 0, "query_setup": 1, "model_gates": 306, "tool_schema_build": 7, "message_normalization": 1, "client_creation": 2, "request_build": 2}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn